Parts derived from Redmine 6.1.2 (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 2006- Jean-Philippe Lang)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- web/templates/: HTML/text templates ported from Redmine's app/views
  (ERB converted to Go templates), including the wiki syntax help pages
  (web/templates/help/). Templates carry no license comments because their
  output must stay byte-identical to Redmine; this NOTICE covers them.
- web/assets/: stylesheets, images, icons (icons.svg), themes (classic,
  alternate), JavaScript (application.js, context_menu.js, gantt.js,
  Stimulus controllers in web/assets/javascript/, jstoolbar, ...) copied from
  Redmine's app/assets, app/javascript and vendor/javascript. Third-party
  libraries bundled there are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
  Assets are synced from the Redmine release named in web/UPSTREAM_VERSION;
  security fixes from later Redmine releases are applied on top of them
  (tools/upstream-patches/: 44429 table_paste_controller.js from 7.0.2), so
  those files deviate from that release.
- web/locales/redmine/: Redmine's translation files (config/locales), copied
  unmodified. At load time Buropher replaces the product name "Redmine" with
  "Buropher" in translation values (internal/brand, internal/i18n).
- web/public/404.html, 500.html: Redmine's static error pages (product name
  replaced).
- internal/settings/settings.yml: Redmine's config/settings.yml (defaults of
  app_title / welcome_text changed to the Buropher name).
- Go code under internal/ and cmd/: business logic, permission model, query
  engine, text formatting (Textile/CommonMark and Redmine links/macros),
  mail handling, SCM integration, PDF/CSV export, REST API and other behavior
  ported from Redmine's app/ and lib/ (Ruby) to Go. Source comments reference
  the Ruby originals.
- internal/textformat/textile/redcloth3.go: port of Redmine's
  lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/textile/redcloth3.rb, itself derived from
  RedCloth 3.0.4 ((c) 2004 why the lucky stiff, BSD license).
- Test data: Redmine's test/fixtures (internal/testfixtures/testdata/redmine,
  internal/mailhandler/testdata, testdata/compat/files, ...) and expected
  outputs generated by running Redmine 6.1.2 (golden files under testdata/
  and internal/*/testdata). The Git fixture repository used by SCM tests
  (Redmine's test/fixtures/repositories/git_repository.tar.gz) is not
  bundled; tests extract it from a local Redmine checkout.

Third-party components
----------------------

Buropher bundles or ports third-party software (JavaScript libraries, fonts,
Rails/doorkeeper translation files, Rouge lexers, Go modules). Their licenses
and the reasoning for GPL compatibility are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

Compatibility identifiers
-------------------------

For compatibility with Redmine clients, mail filters and imported data,
Buropher keeps machine-facing identifiers that contain the name "Redmine"
(for example X-Redmine-* HTTP/mail headers, "redmine." Message-ID prefixes,
the "Redmine" authentication realm, and the `buropher redmine` import/export
commands). See docs/compatibility.md. These are used only for
interoperability and do not imply endorsement.
